<title>ITALY: Italy metalworkers resume pay dispute talks.</title>
<headline>Italy metalworkers resume pay dispute talks.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unions and employers in Italy's engineering and metalworking industry resumed talks on Tuesday, aimed at ending their pay dispute.</p>
<p>Leaders of the sector's three unions -- FIOM, FIM and UILM -- and the director general of the employers' group Federmeccanica, Michele Figurati, were taking part in the talks at the labour ministry.</p>
<p>It was the second day of efforts to try to end the stand-off that has dragged on for months.</p>
<p>Monday's talks were the first for more than a month in the dispute that has already seen three one-day strikes since it began last June.</p>
</text>
